    "body": "Thank you for pointing this out! Previously, callers like WebDriver BiDi's `input.setFiles` had to work around `update the file selection` only taking `element` by writing prose like *\"update the file selection for |element| with |files| as the user's selection\"*, because HTML didn't define a parameter for programmatic paths.\r\n\r\nSince we are updating HTML here, I updated `update the file selection` to accept an optional `paths` parameter (default `null`) and exported it:\r\n- When `paths` is non-null, `selected files` is updated to represent the files at `paths` (or, if a path in `paths` is a directory, all files with that directory as an ancestor, matching WICG Entries API's `webkitdirectory` model); otherwise it continues to represent the user's selection.\r\n- `show the picker, if applicable` now passes `fileDialogBehavior`'s `paths` to `update the file selection` when `fileDialogBehavior` is non-null.",
